00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:17.620
- You guys met how long ago?

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:19.160
- [Tina] Back three years ago?

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:20.940
- [Mike] Three, Yeah. Almost

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:23.133
- [Mark] Mike, tell me about
your childhood in Boston.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.670
- My whole family's from there.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.113
My dad passed away when I was five.

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:32.649
Since then it's been going back there

00:00:32.649 --> 00:00:34.052
in summertimes.

00:00:34.052 --> 00:00:35.650
But I was going back there in summertimes

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:40.120
to see my grandparents, to
live with them for the summers.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:41.450
- [Mark] So you lost your dad early?

00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:42.600
- Yup, yup.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.310
- [Mark] How was your childhood?

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:45.190
- It was good.

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:47.940
It was good, but it was
two separate families.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.010
It was my dad's side.

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:51.170
And then my mom's side and

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:52.270
both sides drank

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:56.120
and this is one side was like

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:57.530
completely different than the other.

00:00:57.530 --> 00:00:58.960
One played cards and

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:01.253
they worked at Boston University.

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:03.410
They were in a union,

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:07.543
I don't know , they just seem
different than my mom's side.

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:11.593
I just remember remembering
that difference.

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:15.530
Sometimes it was a little harder

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:18.770
to be around my mom's side of
the family for some reason.

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:20.710
Not much harder but just different,

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:22.530
in uncomfortable way.

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:24.433
- [Mark] But how would you
describe your childhood?

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:28.673
- It was,

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:33.030
a lot of trying to fit in,

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:34.350
just trying to fit in a lot.

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:36.750
I've felt like I was misplaced.

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:38.210
- [Mark] No serious abuse or?

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:40.340
- No, no, no serious abuse.

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:42.060
Just my mom drinking,

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:44.010
it wasn't in it, when she got drunk

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:46.830
it wasn't bad until like they would fight.

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:48.810
So my stepdad, whom she remarried,

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:50.167
would fight with my mom.

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:52.898
And then once they fought,

00:01:52.898 --> 00:01:54.937
it was like just a bunch of stuff

00:01:54.937 --> 00:01:57.750
and it usually would end up my mom saying,

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.190
I'm leaving, I'm gonna go
kill myself, which is ironic,

00:02:00.190 --> 00:02:02.450
cause I said that a lot to her.

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:03.940
She would leave the house and

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:07.170
I don't know, I remember my mom

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:09.460
not coming back one time

00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:13.463
my little brother,

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:16.760
and I was looking out the window

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:21.290
and like wondering if,
she was gonna come home

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:24.700
like she said, she was
going to kill herself.

00:02:26.210 --> 00:02:27.393
