you guys have learned?

00:25:44.960 --> 00:25:45.793
- Brutal.

00:25:46.760 --> 00:25:48.774
- [Mark] You've been through a lot.

00:25:48.774 --> 00:25:50.924
- What would you say
most important lesson?

00:25:53.640 --> 00:25:55.330
- I know, I know mine.

00:25:55.330 --> 00:25:56.264
Do you wanna go first?

00:25:56.264 --> 00:25:57.097
- No.

00:25:58.277 --> 00:25:59.913
- I've been learning it lately.

00:26:05.470 --> 00:26:08.720
It's about priorities and getting like,

00:26:10.750 --> 00:26:13.623
never letting her go as far as like,

00:26:14.460 --> 00:26:17.400
out of my sight, if I'm
protecting her, but really

00:26:17.400 --> 00:26:18.420
what it boils down to.

00:26:18.420 --> 00:26:19.970
I kinda wanted to be in that position

00:26:19.970 --> 00:26:21.570
if I got my priorities straight.

00:26:22.440 --> 00:26:25.290
I thought, I think like if I have,

00:26:25.290 --> 00:26:26.343
God, family,

00:26:27.240 --> 00:26:28.160
and me,

00:26:28.160 --> 00:26:29.320
or whatever,

00:26:29.320 --> 00:26:32.670
recovery, whatever how you
want to put it in order.

00:26:32.670 --> 00:26:35.703
And I act that way, my
actions, cause I can say it.

00:26:37.040 --> 00:26:39.510
If I tell her I love you,
and my actions don't say

00:26:39.510 --> 00:26:44.180
I love you, then that's the best I can do.

00:26:44.180 --> 00:26:45.653
So like really,

00:26:48.240 --> 00:26:49.370
don't take it for granted.

00:26:49.370 --> 00:26:51.230
Don't take anything for granted,

00:26:51.230 --> 00:26:53.420
like my son, and this and that.

00:26:53.420 --> 00:26:54.820
What's ripping me from that?

00:26:55.970 --> 00:26:58.343
So like I gotta structure my priorities.

00:26:59.764 --> 00:27:01.756
- [Mark] Tina, what
would you say is the most

00:27:01.756 --> 00:27:04.750
important lesson you've learned?

00:27:04.750 --> 00:27:06.290
- Taking responsibility

00:27:06.290 --> 00:27:08.210
isn't always just about,

00:27:08.210 --> 00:27:10.740
like saying I'm taking responsibility

00:27:10.740 --> 00:27:13.983
for my actions or like this
is, you know, it's my fault.

00:27:16.700 --> 00:27:18.150
It means a lot more than that

00:27:19.120 --> 00:27:20.480
because you can be

00:27:22.070 --> 00:27:23.030
response --

00:27:23.030 --> 00:27:23.990
you can think you're

00:27:23.990 --> 00:27:26.190
taking responsibility for
your actions but holding

00:27:26.190 --> 00:27:28.980
a lot of grudges against
people and a lot of hatred

00:27:28.980 --> 00:27:32.193
and resentment that you
don't even know about,

00:27:33.340 --> 00:27:34.203
when in reality,

00:27:35.680 --> 00:27:38.680
you know where you're
at cause you're there

00:27:38.680 --> 00:27:40.530
and you can just

00:27:40.530 --> 00:27:43.680
deal with it or just
continue being angry, and

00:27:45.880 --> 00:27:48.540
making choices that are
gonna, like, he says

00:27:48.540 --> 00:27:49.803
delay the suffering.

00:27:52.830 --> 00:27:54.720
If you just let it go and realize,

00:27:54.720 --> 00:27:59.490
I am where I am, because
that's where God has me now.

00:27:59.490 --> 00:28:01.800
And that's what God
wanted me to go through.

00:28:01.800 --> 00:28:04.393
And you know, it's because
of all of this that,

00:28:05.230 --> 00:28:06.880
I'm where I'm at now, it's a lot.

00:28:07.780 --> 00:28:11.180
It makes the outlook seem not so dim

00:28:11.180 --> 00:28:12.523
because you realize,

00:28:14.370 --> 00:28:15.880
my whole future

00:28:18.720 --> 00:28:20.170
could have been just

00:28:20.170 --> 00:28:22.770
continuing to stack on
these resentment and pain,

00:28:22.770 --> 00:28:24.620
and suffering that you didn't know about.

00:28:24.620 --> 00:28:28.670
But then you get here on the
street, you're brought so low

00:28:28.670 --> 00:28:32.470
to where you're broken and
you kinda open your eyes

00:28:32.470 --> 00:28:36.340
and realize like, I'm
not even mad at them.

00:28:36.340 --> 00:28:37.590
I just need to let that go

00:28:37.590 --> 00:28:38.840
and be okay with me

00:28:40.745 --> 00:28:41.820
and move on from it.

00:28:41.820 --> 00:28:45.820
And it's kind of amazing how
much relief you get from that.

00:28:45.820 --> 00:28:48.173
I mean, it sounds simple, but it's not.

00:28:49.060 --> 00:28:51.220
Because you can say you
got to like be broken

00:28:51.220 --> 00:28:53.175
and get to the bottom of the barrel,

00:28:53.175 --> 00:28:55.508
before you can recover.

00:28:55.508 --> 00:28:56.573
But

00:28:56.573 --> 00:28:58.190
it's very easy to say

00:28:58.190 --> 00:29:01.608
but sometimes the lowest
point that you're at

00:29:01.608 --> 00:29:04.193
you think there's no
worse, it can get worse.

00:29:06.670 --> 00:29:07.670
- [Mark] All right, Mike and Tina,

00:29:07.670 --> 00:29:10.320
Thank you so much for sharing your story.

00:29:10.320 --> 00:29:12.118
I wish you guys the best of
luck out there in the street.

00:29:12.118 --> 00:29:12.951
- Thank you.

00:29:12.951 --> 00:29:14.000
- Thank you very much.

